From: numerical-auditor (Lane N1)
Subject: [patch proposal, not committed] Use std::expm1 to compute 1 - E in JC/MkN/F81 closed forms

Lane N1 audit (dev/red-team/numerical/fast-exp-conditioning.md) found that
the closed-form transition probabilities suffer catastrophic cancellation
when (rate * branch) <= ~1e-10:

  p_diff = inv_k - inv_k * exp(-alpha * t)         [JC]
  one_m_d = 1 - exp(-mu * t)                       [F81]
  P01 / P10 = i01 - i01 * exp(-lambda * t)         [MkN]

Worst observed relative error on the audit grid:

  JC  p_diff   3.9e-1  at rt ~ 1e-15
  F81 1-d     1.7e-1  at mu*t ~ 1e-15
  MkN P01     4.4e-5  at lambda*t = 1e-12

After replacing `1 - exp(arg)` with `-std::expm1(arg)`, all three drop to
<= 2.4e-16 across the entire grid. fast_neg_exp itself is correct (<= 8.6e-15
relative error in [-708, 0]); the issue is purely algebraic.

The patch keeps MKP_EXP for the E-as-such reads (e.g. p_same = inv_k + ...*E)
and only adds one std::expm1 call per branch.

Patch is *not* committed - the auditor lane is read-only on src/.

----- patch begins -----

diff --git a/src/rate_matrix.cpp b/src/rate_matrix.cpp
--- a/src/rate_matrix.cpp
+++ b/src/rate_matrix.cpp
@@ -29,9 +29,12 @@ Rcpp::NumericMatrix jc_transition_probs(int k, double t) {

   Rcpp::NumericMatrix P(k, k);
   double inv_k = 1.0 / k;
-  double exp_term = MKP_EXP(-k * t / (k - 1.0));
-  double diag = inv_k + (1.0 - inv_k) * exp_term;
-  double off_diag = inv_k - inv_k * exp_term;
+  // Use expm1 to avoid catastrophic cancellation in (1 - E) at small rt.
+  double arg = -k * t / (k - 1.0);
+  double neg_expm1 = -std::expm1(arg);          // = 1 - exp(arg), ulp-accurate
+  double exp_term  = 1.0 - neg_expm1;           // = exp(arg)
+  double diag      = inv_k + (1.0 - inv_k) * exp_term;
+  double off_diag  = inv_k * neg_expm1;

   for (int i = 0; i < k; ++i) {
     for (int j = 0; j < k; ++j) {
@@ -75,12 +78,15 @@ Rcpp::NumericMatrix mkn_transition_probs(double rate_loss, double t) {
   double rate01 = 2.0 / sum_rl;
   double rate10 = 2.0 * rate_loss / sum_rl;
   double lambda = rate01 + rate10;
-  double exp_term = MKP_EXP(-lambda * t);
+  // expm1 form avoids cancellation in P01/P10 at small lambda*t.
+  double arg = -lambda * t;
+  double neg_expm1 = -std::expm1(arg);
+  double exp_term  = 1.0 - neg_expm1;

   double inv_lambda_01 = rate01 / lambda;
   double inv_lambda_10 = rate10 / lambda;

   Rcpp::NumericMatrix P(2, 2);
   P(0, 0) = inv_lambda_10 + inv_lambda_01 * exp_term;
-  P(0, 1) = inv_lambda_01 - inv_lambda_01 * exp_term;
-  P(1, 0) = inv_lambda_10 - inv_lambda_10 * exp_term;
+  P(0, 1) = inv_lambda_01 * neg_expm1;
+  P(1, 0) = inv_lambda_10 * neg_expm1;
   P(1, 1) = inv_lambda_01 + inv_lambda_10 * exp_term;

