Performance note: std::expm1 is ~1.5x slower than std::exp and ~3-4x slower
than fast_neg_exp. Each call site already does one MKP_EXP per branch per
class; replacing it with one std::expm1 + one subtract adds an extra ~50%
to the exp-computation cost. The exp computation is a small fraction of
the per-branch loop (k linear ops dominate for k > 4), so the wall-clock
impact is expected to be a few percent at most.

Suggested validation:
  - run tests/testthat at the same numerical tolerance
  - add a regression test at rt = 1e-12 confirming p_diff matches an mpmath
    or explicit Taylor reference to 1e-14
